{
  "title": "Single Number",
  "description": "In the list `nums`, every value appears **exactly twice** except for one value that appears exactly once. Return that value.\n\n### Examples\n\n| `nums` | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[2, 2, 1]` | `1` |\n| `[4, 1, 2, 1, 2]` | `4` |\n| `[1]` | `1` |\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= nums.size() <= 1000`\n- `-2^31 <= nums[i] <= 2^31 - 1`\n- Try to use constant extra memory.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "int single_number(vector<int> nums) {\n    int result = 0;\n    for (int x : nums) {\n        result ^= x;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n",
  "template": "int single_number(vector<int> nums) {\n    // Return the one value that does not appear twice.\n    return 0;\n}\n",
